INC_DESC: Background: The Consumer Finance Operations Verification Team perform income and/or liability verification on applications to assist in meeting our Responsible Lending requirements.  Incident/Factual Summary: On 15/04/2026 a customer submitted Personal Loan application 9543432783.  On 20/04/2026 a CNX Bangalore team member actioned the application and it was approved for $96,000.  On 23/04/2026 during a quality assurance check it was identified that an error had been made during the assessment of the application, at this point the funds had been accessed.  The Bangalore team member verified the customers income incorrectly by manually calculating the Net YTD incorrectly. As there was no YTD value for the post tax deductions we cannot manually calculate the Net YTD therefore the income should be verified through the customers bank statements.  When verifying through the bank statements the application does not meet serviceability requirements.   On the same day the application was reviewed by a Verification Authority Exception Holder (VAEH) team member who was unable to make an exception. The VAEH team member noted the customer seems to have salary packaging which can be included in the assessment under exception after further information is confirmed with the customer.  An attempt to contact the customer has been made on 3 separate occasions however unsuccessful.    Note: - Incident identified through control CTL000147551.   Actions taken to rectify/prevent reoccurrence: 1. VAEH reviewed, and no exception made 23/04. 2. 3 unsuccessful attempts to contact customer made.  3. Review of Support Procedure conducted by Rectification Manager to ensure there is no GAP. Procedure states 'If you cannot calculate the NET YTD, request bank statements or transaction summary listing'. No GAP identified.  4. Feedback and training have been provided to the team member. 5. The Consequence Management Framework has been applied in the form of a discussion between the team leader and team member, this has been documented as a record of discussion.
