INC_NAME: Authorised Third Party not visible in AssistNow causing direct contact with customer and missed hardship outcomes to all parties.
INC_INCDNT_CAUSE: SPECIFIC CAUSE UNDER REVIEW. Response from Senior Engineer re account example 12/6:  As per the information that I have received –  • For customer data to be picked up correctly in PCC, either: o The customer must already be active in PCC and the update must be performed on the same day, or o When a new debt episode is created, the entire customer profile will be refreshed. • An issue arises when a customer/account exists in PCC as inactive, and the same account is received as an update rather than a new record. In this scenario, the customer information is not refreshed. This becomes problematic if the ATP was originally loaded while the account was inactive. • To ensure the information is picked up in such cases: o Update the ATP details after the account is active. o This should trigger the update to be processed in the overnight batch. o This can be done either by reloading the ATP or by making a minor change (e.g., updating a field) to force the refresh.  9/7 Root Cause Analysis: Analysis:  The issue occurs when an account is cured. As part of the cure (Debt Episode End) process, a Groovy script is triggered that end-dates the ATP relationship for the cured account. However, the current logic unintentionally end-dates the ATP relationship across all accounts linked to the same ATP.   In this specific case, ATP details were correctly received from EIG and updated in PCC for customer example. Coincidentally, on the same day, another account belonging to the same customer was cured. During the cure process, the Groovy script executed and incorrectly end-dated the ATP relationship across all accounts associated with that ATP, effectively reversing the ATP update that had been applied earlier.   As a result, whenever any account linked to an ATP is cured, the current logic end-dates ATP relationships across all related accounts/customer in PCC, leading to the ATP no longer being associated with accounts where it should remain active.
